==Appearance==
Gourdy is a young, anthropomorphic pumpkin. At the top of his head, he has a stem and curled leaf, and a seam separates this from the rest of his head. He sports a fanged grin, and his eyes are uniquely distinct in that he has a black sclera and white pupil, resembling the carved eyes of a jack-o'-lantern. He has large paws for hands, with four  claws on each hand, and a long, slim tail (which is curved in-game), with a slightly bent leaf on the tip. His head, torso, and hands are orange, while his arms, legs, claws, and tail are green. His legs gradient into a darker green, matching the tail, and have 6 slim stripes of the original green, resembling a pumpkin vine.

==Personality==
Gourdy is shown to be a very excitable, friendly [[Toon]], with a huge love for Halloween. However, he is also shown to be quite insecure, as he constantly misses his [[Gourdy's Parents|parents]], evidenced by the drawings of them in his bedroom, his Trinket {{TI|Memory Locket|name=true}},  his [[Gossip]] dialogues, and his dialogue when entering the locked lore room in the second Halloween map. In one of said gossip dialogues, he has also pointed out that he tries really hard to be the best face and mascot for Gardenview's Halloween events, alongside the expectations placed upon him as a {{Type|Main}} Toon playing an additional factor into this.

Gourdy demonstrably idolizes the Main Character Toons, perhaps even seeing them as superior to him, an example being his dialogue with {{CI|Vee|name=true}} and his gossip about {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} revealing his deep admiration for the Toons. His room even features plush toys of all the Main Characters, further supporting this. Gourdy also seems to be polite and well-mannered, as evidenced in his dialogue where he frequently addresses other Toons as Mr. or Ms., and calls the Mains by their last names, unless instructed otherwise, with the exception of {{CI|Bobette|name=true}}, though this could be due to them being Main Characters from different holidays. Despite this he tries to like Shelly but doesn't seem to like her as much as the other Mains as seen with his gossip about her.

In one of Gourdy's gossip dialogues about {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}, he seems to be trying to hide how upset he is about his lack of parents, loneliness, and [[Gardenview]] shutting down. He clearly cares more about his friend now that he can't even remember his parents, as well as the fact the Toons are by themselves, so it's likely interacting with Toodles comforts him since they are both children and therefore relate more to each other. He speaks about not seeing her often but tries to stay upbeat and happy about it, though you can clearly sense his anxiety and fear of losing her.

