**In his {{Skin|Crinkling Leaves}} Skin, Gourdy looks like a dried out pumpkin, making his color look more like Mrs. Holloway and his leaves look more like Mr. Holloway.
*In his {{Skin|Midnight Sleeper}} Skin, Gourdy's arms are slightly raised compared to his other skins. Why this change was made is unknown.
*Gourdy is the fourth [[Toon]] to have their Toon and [[Twisted]] counterparts in two separate thumbnails.
*According to Gourdy's gossip about [[Eclipse]], he has a small flame in his head.
**However, he doesn't glow in [[Blackouts]], as the flame would be too small to emit any useful light.
*Gourdy's Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Gourdy|name=true}}, doesn't give [[Stealth]].
*Similar to {{CI|Astro|name=true}}, the aura that is produced when Gourdy uses his Active [[Ability]] is actually a 3d model.
*Gourdy is the [[Main Character]] with the shortest [[Ability]] Cooldown (if not counting [[Bassie]]), with it being 35 seconds.
*Gourdy is the only [[Halloween]] [[Holiday Toons|Toon]] to be able to speak to a [[Christmas]] Toon.
**This is likely due to him and [[Bobette]] being [[Main Characters]], so they have a guaranteed chance to interact with other Holiday Toons.
*Even though his Active [[Ability]] description says it provides a 20% boost, it actually adds 50% to Skill Check chance (totaling to 75% instead of 45%).
*Gourdy received a special Quest labeled '''Gourdy's Quest''' in the [[2026 Halloween Event|Halloween Event]], giving you {{TTI|Locked Away|name=true}}  and a key that unlocks the secret door in the [[Holiday Floors|Halloween Seasonal Floor]].
*Gourdy is the first Shopkeeper [[Toon]] to have a dramatic change to his [[Gourdy's Shop|shop]] dialogues. In the first run of the [[2025 Halloween Event|Halloween Event]], all of his dialogue reflected his excited, child-like nature; in the second run of the [[2026 Halloween Event|Halloween Event]] however, he is noticeably less enthused, using almost no exclamation marks. This could be due to the revelation and new lore drops of his [[Gourdy's Parents|parents]], causing him to become depressed, or him trying to act more mature to fulfill his desire of being a strong leader to the rest of the Halloween Toons and being a [[Main Character]], but the true cause of this is unknown.
**Interestingly, other dialogue outside of his shop wasn't changed, even any dialogue releasing after the change.
*Gourdy may be the other [[Toon]] {{CI|Astro|name=true}} talks about when {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} opens up to him about missing a part of him. This makes sense with how both were missing a core person in their personality, with Sprout missing {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} and Gourdy missing his parents.
*Gourdy's walk animation may be based off of {{CI|Twisted Bobette|name=true}} but sped up, as it is very similar.
*Gourdy is the only [[Main Character]] to lack a selfish Ability, as both of his Abilities benefit his teammates.
*Gourdy often refers to [[Toons]] with honorifics, likely to show respect for his elders. Despite this, he doesn't do so for all of them. As for the base-game [[Main Characters]], he refers to them by their last name as well, except for [[Pebble]] and [[Vee]].
**The other [[Halloween Toons]], [[Connie]], and [[Toodles]] are his friends, so he'd naturally speak more casually with them. Additionally, Toodles is a child like Gourdy.
**[[Bobette]] is a [[Christmas Toon]], leading to a more disconnected and awkward relationship between the two, as they're from different Holidays.
**Pebble is the equivalent of a dog, which aren't typically referred to with honorifics.
**It's unknown whether Vee's last name (Version 1) or Gourdy's sheer excitement was the reason for the lack of an honorific for her.
**Gourdy directly states that he drank a large quantity of {{II|Pop|name=false}} prior to speaking to {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}, with the sheer hyperactivity caused by the beverage possibly disrupting his polite demeanor.
*Gourdy is the first [[Toon]] to have one of their [[Skins]] released as a plush in the official store.<ref>https://dandysworld.gg/collections/gourdy/products/lost-prince-gourdy-deluxe-plush</ref>
**Additionally, the plush comes with a variation of his [[Trinket]], [[Memory Locket]], so he is the first one to have an alternate version of their Trinket come out, albeit it's not in-game.
**There is also a {{Skin|Dino Snore|toon={{CI|Shelly|name=true}}}} plush in some stores, though it isn't sold in the official Dandy's World Store.
*As revealed in the Queens of Mischief music video and [[Changelog|v0.29.7]] thumbnail, Gourdy can play a drum kit.
*Gourdy's dialogue with {{CI|Squirm|name=true}} references the [https://www.roblox.com/bundles/201/Headless-Horseman Headless Horseman] bundle.
*Gourdy's dialogue with [[Blot]] reveals that the two of them can use the latter's mime performances as a way of communication, though the former is still learning.
*Gourdy's dialogue with [[Toodles]] reveals that he wants to play the role of the villain, though this is likely done in a playful manner to trick the other toons rather than out of malice, proven by [[Gourdy's Shop#Gossip|Gourdy's Shop Gossip]] about [[Squirm]], saying that he wants to be fun-scary, not scary-scary.

